---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import wire from '../../wire.json';

const all = wire.groups.flatMap(g => g.sources);
const withUrl = all.filter(s => s.url);
const linked = all.filter(s => s.verified === true && s.url);
const checked = all.some(s => s.lastChecked);
---
<Base title="The Wire" description="Every source FinOpine reads before forming a view." path="/wire/">
  <div class="eyebrow">The Wire</div>
  <h1 class="art-title">Everything read before a view is formed.</h1>
  <p class="art-dek">
    Ordered from primary to interpretation. If an argument on this site rests on
    a number, it should be traceable to something in the first two groups.
  </p>

  <div class="note">
    <b>A source is a link only once the URL has been confirmed live.</b><br />
    {linked.length} of {withUrl.length} have been. The rest are listed by name
    without a link, because a name you can search is more use than a link that
    404s. {!checked && <>No check has been run yet — run <b>npm run check:wire</b>.</>}
  </div>

  {wire.groups.map((g) => (
    <div class="wire-grp">
      <h3>{g.name}</h3>
      <p class="why">{g.why}</p>
      <ul>
        {g.sources.map((s) => (
          <li>
            <span class={s.tier === 'daily' ? 'tier p' : 'tier'}>{s.tier}</span>
            <b>
              {s.verified && s.url
                ? <a href={s.url} rel="noopener">{s.name}</a>
                : s.name}
            </b>
            {s.what && <span>{s.what}</span>}
          </li>
        ))}
      </ul>
    </div>
  ))}

  <div class="note">
    <b>Why so few links.</b><br />
    Every URL here was copied from a live search result, never written from
    memory — a model reconstructs the shape of a plausible URL rather than
    recalling a real one, which is how sites end up citing pages that have never
    existed. Sources that could not be confirmed that way are listed unlinked
    rather than guessed at. In fintech that trade is not close.
  </div>
</Base>
